        "original_id": "ae168d0f-4700-5c11-800c-d76538fdb96f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William Hawkins Polk, James K. Polk\n- Roles: United States House of Representatives member, President of the United States\n- Places: Tennessee's 6th congressional district, United States\n\nFacts:\n- James Knox Polk was born on November 2, 1795, and he served as the 11th President of the United States from 1845 to 1849.\n- William Hawkins Polk was born on May 24, 1815, and he was the younger brother of President James K. Polk.\n- William Hawkins Polk was an American politician who served in the United States House of Representatives for Tennessee's 6th congressional district from 1851 to 1853.\n- William Hawkins Polk died on December 16, 1862.",
